"""TPS22919 — TI 5.5 V, 1.5 A load switch with controlled slew rate and QOD, SC-70-6 (DCK).

One gated power rail: the TPS22919 plus the passives its datasheet application
circuit (Figure 30) calls for — input bypass, local output bypass, the QOD
strap that sets the off-state discharge path, and an external ON pull-down
that makes "off" the powered-up default.

Variant selection (`automotive`)

    automotive  MPN                 Grade                 Alternates
    False       TPS22919DCKR        catalog, -40 to 105 C  TPS22919DCKT (250-pc T&R)
    True        TPS22919QDCKRQ1     AEC-Q100 grade 1       —

Both are SC-70-6 (DCK), pin-identical (1=IN, 2=GND, 3=ON, 4=NC, 5=QOD,
6=OUT), and carry the same electrical and switching specifications
(TPS22919 SLVSENSB §6 vs the TPS22919-Q1 datasheet §6); only qualification
and guaranteed ambient range differ.

Slew rate is fixed silicon on this device — TI ships no pin-compatible
SC-70-6 sibling with a different rise time or a different internal QOD
resistance. The adjustable-rise-time relatives (TPS22917, TPS22918, with a
CT pin) are SOT-23-6 with a different pinout, so they need their own
package. Configure fall time here with `discharge` / `r_qod`.

Operating envelope (SLVSENSB §6.1, §6.3, §6.5)
- VIN 1.6 V to 5.5 V (abs max 6 V). VOUT tracks VIN when enabled.
- 1.5 A continuous, 2.5 A pulsed (2 ms, 2 % duty).
- R_ON 89 mOhm typ at 5 V, 90 mOhm at 3.6 V, 105 mOhm at 1.8 V;
  150 mOhm max at 5 V over -40 to 85 C.
- Self-protected: I_SC 3 A typ into a soft short, folded back to 500 mA typ
  once VIN - VOUT exceeds V_SC (0.36 V typ), 2 us response, then thermal
  shutdown at 180 C with 35 C hysteresis. There is no fault flag output.
- R_theta_JA is 210.7 C/W in this package (§6.4), so dissipation dominates
  the usable current, not R_ON: 1.5 A continuous burns 0.34 W at 150 mOhm
  and lifts T_J by ~71 C. Loads up to a few hundred mA are thermally free
  (360 mA -> 54 mV drop, 19 mW, ~4 C rise).

ON control (§8.3.1)
- V_IH >= 1 V, V_IL <= 0.35 V, referenced to GND and independent of VIN, so
  a 3.3 V GPIO can gate a 5 V rail directly. Abs max V_ON is 6 V.
- The internal Smart Pull Down (530 kOhm typ) holds ON low only until ON is
  first driven high, after which it disconnects to save power. The pin
  table still says "do not leave floating".
- R_ON_PD (100 kOhm default, populated) is the reason this package is
  default-off without an override: it holds ON at GND while the controlling
  MCU is in reset, unprogrammed, or driving high-Z, and it survives the
  Smart Pull Down disconnecting. Cost is V_GPIO / 100 kOhm of extra drive
  current while enabled (33 uA at 3.3 V, 55 uA at 5.5 V) against the 8 uA
  typ I_Q. Set `on_pulldown_resistance` higher, or `on_pulldown=False` to
  depopulate, only if that current matters more than the defined off state.

Inrush and turn-on (§6.6, §9.2.2.1)
- Fixed slew rate: 3.2 mV/us at 5 V, 2.7 mV/us at 3.6 V, 1.8 mV/us at
  1.8 V; t_ON 1.95 ms / 1.75 ms / 1.5 ms respectively.
- Inrush = C_L x SR (Eq 3): 3.2 mA into the default 1 uF at 5 V, 32 mA into
  10 uF, 150 mA into the datasheet's 47 uF example. Size total downstream
  bulk from the inrush the upstream rail can absorb.

Output discharge (§8.3.3, Table 2)
- `discharge="Internal"` (default): R_QOD is a 0 Ohm strap, so QOD sits on
  VOUT and the internal 24 Ohm pull-down (R_PD,QOD) discharges the rail.
  t_FALL = 2.2 x (R_DIS || R_L) x C_L (Eq 2) -> ~53 us for 1 uF unloaded.
  This is the right default for a rail that must be provably dead when
  gated off; leaving the output floating keeps residual charge on it.
- `discharge="External"`: R_QOD is populated with `r_qod` in series, so
  R_DIS = 24 Ohm + r_qod (Eq 1) and the fall is slowed for power-down
  sequencing. The 1 kOhm default is the datasheet's own §9.2.2.3 example
  point (47 uF, ~40 ms fall).
- `discharge="Off"`: R_QOD is depopulated, QOD floats, and VOUT is left
  floating when the switch opens.

Off state
- I_SD 2 nA typ, 800 nA max over temperature (§6.5) — a real off, not a
  low-power mode.
- No reverse blocking. The pass NMOS body diode is oriented OUT -> IN
  (§8.2 block diagram), so back-driving VOUT above VIN feeds current into
  the input rail whatever ON is doing.

Integrator-owned
- Downstream bulk/decoupling beyond the local C_OUT, and any upstream bulk
  the rail needs to absorb the turn-on step (§10 asks for at least the
  1 uF C_IN provided here, more if the supply is slow).
- GPIO series/ESD parts on ON, and the ON net's own routing.
- Placement: keep C_IN and C_OUT at the device pins with wide VIN/VOUT/GND
  copper (§11.1). The bundled layout fragment does this.

Footprint: KiCad stock `SOT-363_SC-70-6` (JEDEC MO-203 variant AB) with
embedded STEP, the same land pattern used by the SN74LVC2G14DCKR package in
this registry. Pads are 1.025 x 0.35 mm on a 1.675 mm span versus TI's
DCK0006A recommendation of 0.9 x 0.4 mm on a 2.2 mm span (both reach the
same 3.1 mm outer envelope); the KiCad pattern trades toe extension for
heel coverage and is IPC-7351 nominal density.
"""

load("@stdlib/checks.zen", "voltage_within")
load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Capacitance", "Resistance")

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")

Discharge = enum("Internal", "External", "Off")

automotive = config(bool, default=False, help="Select the AEC-Q100 TPS22919QDCKRQ1 instead of the catalog part.")
discharge = config(Discharge, default="Internal", help="Quick output discharge path (datasheet Table 2).")
r_qod = config(Resistance, default="1kohm", help="Series QOD resistance when discharge=External.")
c_in = config(Capacitance, default="1uF", help="Input bypass at IN (datasheet §10 minimum).")
c_out = config(Capacitance, default="1uF", help="Local output bypass; also sets inrush (I = C x SR).")
on_pulldown = config(bool, default=True, help="Populate the external ON pull-down that forces the off state.")
on_pulldown_resistance = config(Resistance, default="100kohm", help="External ON pull-down value.")

VIN = io(Power(voltage="1.6V to 5.5V"))
VOUT = io(Power, help="Switched output; tracks VIN when ON is high.")
GND = io(Ground)
ON = io(Net, help="Active-high enable, V_IH >= 1 V regardless of VIN. Held low by R_ON_PD when undriven.")

voltage_within("1.6V to 5.5V", name="vin_range")(VIN)

# VOUT is a pass-through of VIN, so any declared output voltage must sit inside
# the input's range. Silent when the parent leaves VOUT's voltage undeclared.
if VIN.voltage:
    voltage_within(VIN.voltage, name="vout_matches_vin")(VOUT)

_QOD = Net("QOD")

_CATALOG = Part(mpn="TPS22919DCKR", manufacturer="Texas Instruments")
_CATALOG_ALT = Part(mpn="TPS22919DCKT", manufacturer="Texas Instruments")
_AUTOMOTIVE = Part(mpn="TPS22919QDCKRQ1", manufacturer="Texas Instruments", qualifications=["AEC-Q100"])

Component(
    name="U1",
    symbol=Symbol(
        library="TPS22919.kicad_sym",
        name="TPS22919QDCKRQ1" if automotive else "TPS22919DCKR",
    ),
    part=_AUTOMOTIVE if automotive else _CATALOG,
    properties={"alternatives": [] if automotive else [_CATALOG_ALT]},
    pins={
        "IN": VIN,
        "GND": GND,
        "ON": ON,
        "QOD": _QOD,
        "OUT": VOUT,
    },
)

# 10 V X7R in 0402 is the house 1 uF part. At 5 V bias expect roughly a third
# to a half of nameplate capacitance; that only slows the (already 1.75 ms)
# turn-on support and lowers inrush, so it is acceptable here. Move to 0603/
# 16 V or higher if a rail needs guaranteed effective capacitance.
Capacitor(name="C_IN", value=c_in, voltage="10V", package="0402", P1=VIN, P2=GND)
Capacitor(name="C_OUT", value=c_out, voltage="10V", package="0402", P1=VOUT, P2=GND)

# QOD strap: 0 ohm ties QOD to VOUT for the internal 24 ohm discharge, r_qod
# slows the fall (R_DIS = 24 ohm + r_qod, Eq 1), depopulated leaves VOUT floating.
Resistor(
    name="R_QOD",
    value=r_qod if discharge == Discharge("External") else Resistance("0ohm"),
    package="0402",
    P1=VOUT,
    P2=_QOD,
    dnp=discharge == Discharge("Off"),
)

Resistor(
    name="R_ON_PD",
    value=on_pulldown_resistance,
    package="0402",
    P1=ON,
    P2=GND,
    dnp=not on_pulldown,
)

Layout(name="TPS22919", path="layout/TPS22919")

